 ### Implicit Neural Point Clouds (INPC)
-Uses implicit fields to represent point features, allowing for smoother interpolation and handling of sparse data, whereas NPR-MPP uses explicit multi-plane projection [S2, unofficial].
+Represents point features using implicit fields rather than explicit multi-plane projection. When to choose: Not given in the sources. Link: [Implicit Neural Point Clouds (INPC)](18226-implicit-neural-point-clouds-inpc.md).
 
 ### Point Cloud Inpainting via Gate/Sparse Convolution
-Focuses on repairing missing parts of point clouds using sparse convolutions, a preprocessing or postprocessing step rather than a direct rendering method [S2, unofficial].
+Repairs missing parts of point clouds using sparse convolutions. When to choose: Not given in the sources. Link: [Point Cloud Inpainting via Gate/Sparse Convolution](15517-point-cloud-inpainting-via-gate-sparse-convolution.md).
 
